# Design tokens and styling

Prefer design tokens (color, space, type, breakpoints) over raw values when a token exists. Tokens live in one place and are exposed so every styling system in the app can use them. If no token fits, say why, or add a token when the value repeats.

Use one styling system per component. Do not mix utility classes and a CSS module in the same component. Component styles stay next to the component. Global styles are imported once from the root layout.

Do not use `!important` unless there is no practical alternative, such as a third-party rule you cannot change. When you use it, say why and what you considered. Avoid deep nesting and id selectors.
